+### 2026-10-10 - process-local shell selection with ACP capability readback
+
+- Reason: on Windows the shared resolver prefers PowerShell, so a host that requires Bash cannot select it for mcode's own foreground and background command tools, and an ACP client cannot verify which interpreter the CLI actually uses.
+- Affected package: `packages/coding-agent` (`@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent`), `src/utils/shell.ts` shell resolution; reported through `packages/tui/src/acp/agent.ts` ACP initialize metadata.
+- Change type: generic, upstreamable. `MCODE_SHELL_PATH` selects an existing absolute shell executable when no explicit argument is supplied; a missing, relative or non-file value raises an error instead of falling back to the platform default. The same resolved value drives command execution and the environment description. ACP initialize reports `_meta["minimax-code/shell"]` with version 1, the resolved executable, its arguments and shell type while the override is present. Permission modes, approval decisions, sandbox policy and the recorded account state are unchanged.
+- Upstream PR: not opened; the interface proposal is published as https://github.com/MiniMax-AI/minimax-code/issues/474.
+- Validation: `packages/local-runtime/test/unit/local-bash-shell-path.test.ts`, registered in the `capability` suite, covers rejection of relative, empty and missing overrides, real Bash identity with a nonzero exit status through `createLocalBashOperations`, cancellation cleanup of the owned descendant, and timeout stdout and stderr streaming. Vendored upstream suites remain outside this distribution's verification, and no live model service is called.
+
 ### 2026-10-06 — opt-in fallback for unexpected provider tool calls
 
 - Reason: a conversational host can intentionally advertise no tools, but a provider may still emit a structured tool call. The normal missing-tool result starts another model hop and can leave the host without a final assistant response.
